# UI Design System Rules (Strict)

Goal: Every page (home, hubs, error/fix pages) must look like one cohesive product.
No “unstyled HTML dumps”. No massive blue-link paragraphs. No random spacing.

## 0) Non-Negotiables
- Use Tailwind classes for all NEW components and UI elements.
- Do NOT rely on browser default styling for lists, headings, links, code blocks.
- All pages MUST use the shared layout shell components below (PageShell + SiteHeader + SiteFooter) **unless explicitly exempted**.
- Primary CTA (“Check domain” / “Re-check SPF/DKIM/DMARC”) must be visually obvious and above the fold.

### Legacy Page Exception
Some existing pages (hub pages and certain error pages) currently use inline styles for layout stability.

Cursor must NOT:
- refactor inline styles into Tailwind
- rewrite layout styling
- restructure existing page layout

Inline styles may remain on legacy pages.

Tailwind must be used for:
- new components
- new pages
- reusable UI elements

## 1) Required shared components (must exist and be used)
Create these components if missing, and use them on ALL new pages:

1) `components/layout/SiteHeader.tsx`
   - Brand left (logo + “Email DNS Check”)
   - Top nav right (SPF / DKIM / DMARC)
   - Sticky optional, but consistent height and spacing.

2) `components/layout/SiteFooter.tsx`
   - 3 columns: SPF Hub links, DKIM Hub links, DMARC Hub links
   - Bottom row: Privacy / Terms / Contact
   - No giant link lists in the page body if they belong in footer.

3) `components/layout/PageShell.tsx`
   - Wraps content with:
     - `min-h-screen`
     - centered container `max-w-5xl` (or `max-w-6xl`)
     - consistent paddings (mobile + desktop)
     - consistent vertical rhythm: sections spaced with `space-y-10` (or similar)

4) `components/ui/Prose.tsx`
   - A controlled typography wrapper (your own, not raw markdown defaults).
   - It should define heading sizes, paragraph line-height, link styling, list styling, code styling.
   - IMPORTANT: This component must prevent the “blue underline everywhere” look.
   - Links inside Prose: use a branded style (e.g., underline on hover, not always).

5) `components/ui/CodeBlock.tsx`
   - Used for all DNS record examples and “One-Minute Fix”.
   - Must have:
     - dark background
     - monospace font
     - horizontal scroll on mobile
     - optional “Copy” button

6) `components/ui/Callout.tsx`
   - Used for warnings (“Common mistakes”), tips, and “What we checked”.
   - Variants: `info`, `warning`, `success`, `danger` with subtle backgrounds.

## 2) Page layout rules (applies to Home, Hub, Error/Fix pages)
Every NEW page should follow this structure:

A) Top: `SiteHeader`

B) Main content (inside PageShell)

1. Breadcrumbs (small)
2. H1 + 1–2 sentence subheading
3. Primary CTA block (Domain checker or Re-check button)
4. “Quick answer / One-Minute Fix” section (must be above the fold on desktop)
5. “How it works / Why it matters” (scannable)
6. “Common mistakes” (Callout)
7. “Next steps” (3 links max)
8. Related fixes (3–6 cards, NOT a paragraph of links)

C) Bottom: `SiteFooter`

## 3) Navigation & internal links (visual rules)
- Do NOT output long inline link paragraphs like:
  “LinkA LinkB LinkC LinkD …”

- Related links must be displayed as:
  - a short bulleted list with spacing OR
  - a grid of cards (preferred)

- Each list item must have:
  - title
  - short description (1 line)

No naked links.

## 4) Typography & spacing rules (consistency)
- Body text max width: `max-w-prose` inside the content area.
- Paragraph line height: `leading-7`.
- Headings:
  - H1: large and bold, consistent across pages
  - H2: clear separation with spacing above
- Lists must have intentional spacing: `space-y-2` minimum.
- Never allow sections to touch: use consistent `py-10` or `space-y-10`.

## 5) Buttons & inputs (design rules)
- Primary button uses the brand yellow.
- Inputs must have consistent height, border, focus ring.
- No tiny default HTML inputs.
- CTA block should be a “card” with border + subtle shadow.

## 6) Don’ts (hard bans)
- BAN: unstyled `<ul><li><a>` dumps without Tailwind.
- BAN: link walls inside a single paragraph.
- BAN: mixing multiple visual styles across pages.
- BAN: adding new “one-off” styling that isn’t reusable via components.

## 7) Definition of Done (UI)

A page is acceptable only if:

- It uses PageShell + SiteHeader + SiteFooter (unless it is a legacy page exempted above).
- The “One-Minute Fix” is in a styled CodeBlock.
- Related fixes appear as cards or a spaced list (not a link wall).
- On mobile: no horizontal overflow except inside CodeBlock.